  "FOR_REVIEW": [
    {
      "point": "A committee may decide ordinary resolutions only, and any other category is refused on a committee agenda with the words in MEETING_RULES.committeeCategoryRefusal.",
      "where": "MEETING_RULES.committeeCategories, committeeCategoryRefusal",
    },
    {
      "point": "For voting, a lot owes the body corporate money when it has an issued contribution notice past its due date and not paid in full, on the building's today.",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/debtor-voting-repo.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "An owner of several lots is refused a vote only if every one of their lots owes money.",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/debtor-voting-repo.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "The draft AGM template and motion library: their wording, and putting the accounts and insurance review motions as ordinary resolutions (no type is recorded for those two).",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/templates.ts QLD_AGM_TEMPLATE, QLD_MOTION_LIBRARY",
    },
    {
      "point": "Pre-meeting electronic voting is not offered for Queensland buildings until it is designed.",
      "where": "MEETING_RULES.preMeetingEvoting",
    },
    {
      "point": "A majority resolution is offered on the agenda but not in the motions list, which does not record written votes without proxies.",
      "where": "MEETING_RULES.motionCategories",
    },
    {
      "point": "At conduct the count decides: where the chair's outcome differs from the count of the votes recorded, nothing is stored and the chair is told what the count gives. There is no override with a reason. A vote from a lot owing money is not counted, and the chair is told which lots, rather than the whole record being refused.",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/conduct-tally.ts outcomeDisagreement, buildConductTally",
    },
    {
      "point": "A special or majority resolution is not counted while the building's number of lots is not recorded or differs from the lots entered, and a lot owing money is left out of the lots entitled to vote on a majority resolution (Act s 107; SM s 102(2)). Money owed is judged on the meeting's date in the building's time zone; that this is the right day is not confirmed.",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/conduct-tally.ts buildConductTally, conduct-actions.ts recordCountedOutcome",
    },
    {
      "point": "Abstentions are not counted as votes cast, so two thirds of the votes cast (Act s 106(3)(a)) is two thirds of the votes for and against. The notes do not define votes cast.",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/rules.ts TWO_THIRDS_LOTS_AND_ENTITLEMENT_CAPS, conduct-tally.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "For voting, a lot owes money only on a contribution notice past its due date with a balance outstanding. A posted late payment penalty or recovery costs (SM ss 165, 166) owed on their own do not make the lot a debtor yet. The penalty was left out because its posting and split are changing in receipting.",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/debtor-voting-repo.ts lotsOwingMoney",
    },
    {
      "point": "A resolution without dissent with no votes cast counts as carried, as the engine reads Act s 105 (no vote against).",
      "where": "src/lib/meetings/rules.ts NO_AGAINST",
    },
    {
      "point": "The draft Queensland debt recovery steps, their labels and their guidance: the step types and order, the wording, who acts, and which steps are StrataVerze practice (ledger check, contact, reminder, final notice, waiver request, referral and closing).",
      "where": "DEBT_RECOVERY_STEPS, DEBT_RECOVERY_STEP_LABELS, DEBT_RECOVERY_GUIDANCE",
    },
    {
      "point": "The 2 year warning: a lot is flagged once its oldest unpaid contribution has been outstanding for 2 years from its date for payment and no proceedings are recorded (no case with the proceedings step completed or a court file number), with the deadline shown as that date plus 2 years and 2 months. It is a warning on the adviser debt recovery page and a daily reminder.",
      "where": "src/lib/debt-recovery/proceedings-deadline.ts, adviser debt recovery page",
    },
    {
      "point": "The 2 year reminder: the advisers and the committee are emailed when a lot is first flagged, at 30, 14 and 7 days before the deadline, and once after it has passed, until proceedings are recorded. A missed day sends one email for the latest point only, and a stage with no email sent is tried again the next day. The subject and heading call the deadline the StrataVerze date (DEBT_RECOVERY.proceedingsReminder), and the email says it is StrataVerze's reading of the rule.",
      "where": "src/lib/debt-recovery/proceedings-reminder.ts, proceedings-reminder-run.ts, DEBT_RECOVERY.proceedingsReminder",
    },
    {
      "point": "The 2 year reminder is not sent for a deadline that passed more than 30 days before the run, so a building's first run at go-live sends no burst about deadlines long gone. Those lots are shown on the adviser debt recovery page only, and get no email.",
      "where": "src/lib/debt-recovery/proceedings-reminder.ts PASSED_REMINDER_WITHIN_DAYS",
    },
    {
      "point": "The 2 year reminder leaves out the lot's owners as the case actions do: an OWNER membership of the lot, active or ended in the last 30 days. Not covered: an owner of several lots whose membership names another lot (a membership holds one lot), a company owner's directors or officers, and an attorney under a power of attorney for the owner. Any of them on the committee is sent the reminder.",
      "where": "src/lib/debt-recovery/lot-owners.ts lotOwnerIds, proceedings-reminder-run.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "Proceedings count only on an open case. A case closed after judgment (for example CLOSED_SETTLED while enforcement is outside StrataVerze) with the contribution still unpaid counts as no proceedings, so the lot is flagged and reminded again. Left as it is for review.",
      "where": "src/lib/debt-recovery/proceedings-deadline.ts lotDebtsFrom",
    },
    {
      "point": "No StrataVerze fee is marked never recoverable from the owner for Queensland: a recovery step fee follows the price book, and owners are told it may be recoverable if reasonably incurred (SM s 166(1)(c)). Whether a StrataVerze fee is such a cost is not confirmed.",
      "where": "NEVER_RECOVERABLE_FEE_VARIANTS, RECOVERY_COSTS_RECOVERABLE",
    },
    {
      "point": "The waiver request step (HARDSHIP_REVIEW) is assigned to the committee, with approval required, although whether the committee can decide a waiver (SM s 166(6)) or a general meeting resolution is needed is not confirmed.",
      "where": "DEBT_RECOVERY_STEPS HARDSHIP_REVIEW",
    },
    {
      "point": "The body corporate certificate headings StrataVerze drafts (from the SM s 233AA(1) contents as summarised in the research notes, ending with anything else in the approved form), their order, the wording of each draft and the execution box. BCCM Form 33 itself was not read.",
      "where": "CERTIFICATE.items, execution, executionLines; src/lib/records/certificate-draft.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "The repeat certificate fee applies when a certificate for the same lot was issued within the previous 3 months to a requester with the same name (letter case and spaces ignored).",
      "where": "src/lib/records/fees.ts certificateFeeFor",
    },
    {
      "point": "The 5 business days for a certificate and the 7 days for access to the records are counted from the day the written request was received, as if the fee came with it. Business days skip weekends only.",
      "where": "CERTIFICATE.giveWithinBusinessDays, INSPECTIONS.accessWithinDays",
    },
    {
      "point": "For access to the records, only an owner pays the owner's fee. An agent, even an owner's agent, pays the fee for anyone else. Copies are charged per page at the year's dollar amount, and the fee is worked out when the access is recorded as given.",
      "where": "INSPECTIONS.ownerFeeTypes; src/lib/records/fees.ts accessFee",
    },
    {
      "point": "The document library shows minutes and insurance policies as kept without a limit (as decided), by-laws without a limit as a record of current relevance, and financial, compliance, other and unlisted categories as kept for at least 6 years, the longer disposal period, although some records in them (reconciliation statements, insignificant correspondence) may be disposed of after 2.",
      "where": "DOCUMENT_RETENTION",
    },
    {
      "point": "Copies are charged at the guidance's dollar amount per page (75 cents in 2026-27) times the pages. SM s 233(7) rounds a fee to the nearest 5 cents: if the fee is 0.65 fee units times the pages, rounded once on the total, a large copy job can differ by a few cents from the per page amount.",
      "where": "src/lib/records/fees.ts accessFee",
    },
    {
      "point": "The dollar amounts for a Queensland certificate or records access are those for the financial year in which the written request was received (SM s 233 ties the fee to the request), not the day it is issued or given.",
      "where": "src/lib/records/records-store.ts issueCertificate, completeInspection",
    },
    {
      "point": "Works approvals compare the quoted total (including any GST) with the major spending limit, worked out from the building's recorded number of lots.",
      "where": "WORKS_QUOTES; src/lib/works/quote-rule.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "The regulation module is a building setting the adviser (or StrataVerze) saves, like the building's name, not part of the locked building record. Only the Standard Module can be saved. The other modules are listed but cannot be chosen.",
      "where": "REGULATION_MODULE; src/app/(portal)/adviser/schemes/actions.ts saveRegulationModuleAction",
    },
    {
      "point": "Each lot's interest schedule lot entitlement is part of the locked building record, as unit entitlement is: once the lot exists only StrataVerze enters or changes it. It is required when a lot is created or imported, and an existing lot may be saved without it (the lot stays flagged).",
      "where": "src/lib/auth/building-lock.ts LOCKED_LOT_FIELDS; src/app/(portal)/adviser/schemes/[id]/lots/actions.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "The share of the buildings insurance premium is decided by the interest schedule for a building recorded as a building or volumetric format plan, and by no schedule for a standard format plan or a building with no plan format recorded (SM s 201(1)). The plan format is recorded once for the whole building, so a scheme whose lots are on more than one kind of plan is not catered for.",
      "where": "PLAN_FORMAT; ENTITLEMENT_SCHEDULES INTEREST decides; src/lib/jurisdiction/building-data.ts scheduleFor",
    },
    {
      "point": "A Queensland building with no module recorded, or with a lot that has no interest schedule lot entitlement, is flagged to the adviser on the building and lot pages and in the certificate draft. Meetings still run on the contribution schedule, which every lot holds. A contribution that includes insurance is refused until every lot has an interest schedule lot entitlement and a building or volumetric format plan is recorded.",
      "where": "src/lib/jurisdiction/building-data.ts; src/lib/levies/contribution-shares.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "The adjustments SM s 201(2) allows to the shares of the buildings insurance premium are not offered. Each lot's share of the insurance part is in proportion to its interest schedule lot entitlement, with no adjustment.",
      "where": "CONTRIBUTION_INSURANCE; src/lib/levies/contribution-shares.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "Insurance means the whole of every line of the fund's adopted budget whose account is an insurance account (account 5-1100, Insurance, in the chart StrataVerze sets up). That whole amount is shared by the interest schedule, and the rest of the contribution, after any other income the adviser allowed for, by the contribution schedule. Insurance booked to another account is shared with the rest. Whether other insurance (for example office bearers or workers cover) is part of insurance under SM s 162(5) is not confirmed.",
      "where": "CONTRIBUTION_INSURANCE; src/lib/levies/contribution-insurance.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "An ordinary contribution to the administrative fund is refused when its adopted budget has no insurance line. This is a StrataVerze choice, not a rule of law: SM s 160(2) has the budget estimate insurance, and a budget without it is taken as a mistake. A sinking fund contribution has no insurance part, and one whose budget has an insurance line is refused, as insurance is paid from the administrative fund (SM s 169(2)).",
      "where": "CONTRIBUTION_INSURANCE.insuranceLineRequired, paidFrom; src/lib/levies/contribution-shares.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "A special contribution (SM s 162(2)) is shared by the contribution schedule only, even when it pays for insurance, since it has no budget lines to show an insurance part.",
      "where": "src/lib/levies/contribution-insurance.ts",
    },
    {
      "point": "The voluntary insurance scheme a basic scheme of standard format lots may adopt (SM s 204) is not offered. A standard format plan can be recorded, but contributions that include insurance are refused for it.",
      "where": "PLAN_FORMAT STANDARD",
    },
    {
      "point": "A contribution that includes insurance is refused outright for a standard format plan. That is stricter than the law: SM s 197(4) would still share the common property and assets premium by the interest schedule, and only the buildings premium goes by reinstatement cost (s 201(1)). StrataVerze refuses because the budget holds insurance as one amount, so the two premiums cannot be told apart.",
      "where": "PLAN_FORMAT STANDARD; CONTRIBUTION_INSURANCE.uses",
    },
    {
      "point": "The plan format is a building setting the adviser (or StrataVerze) saves, like the regulation module, not part of the locked building record. A change applies to contributions raised after it, never to notices already created.",
      "where": "PLAN_FORMAT; src/app/(portal)/adviser/schemes/actions.ts savePlanFormatAction",
    },
    {
      "point": "A payment goes to the penalty first (SM s 166(5)), so an owner who pays only the contribution after a month mark still owes the part of the contribution the penalty took. That part keeps attracting penalty each month until it is paid, even when it is a few dollars. StrataVerze charges it as StrataVerze reads SM ss 165 and 166(5), and does not waive it. Whether that reading is right, whether to tell the owner when it happens, and whether to suggest a waiver for special reasons (s 166(6)), are for review.",
      "where": "PAYMENT_ALLOCATION_ORDER",
    },
    {
      "point": "When a payment or owner credit is applied, the penalty to the payment date is charged first, with its own journal dated the day it is recorded. A payment dated on a month mark is paid within that month. A payment dated after the building's today is refused, and one entered late with an earlier date pays only the penalty accrued by that date.",
      "where": "PAYMENT_ALLOCATION_ORDER; src/lib/finance/levy-receipts.ts, owner-credits.ts applyOwnerCredit",
    },
    {
      "point": "The order is applied within each notice. Which notice a payment goes to is the adviser's choice, and owner credit goes to the earliest due notice first. Whether SM s 166(5) needs every penalty on the lot paid before any contribution is not confirmed.",
      "where": "PAYMENT_ALLOCATION_ORDER; src/lib/finance/owner-credit.ts planCreditApplication",
    },
    {
      "point": "An agreed arrangement to pay overdue contributions is called a "Payment Arrangement", not a payment plan, because Queensland has no statutory payment plan. Where an owner's Queensland and NSW lots are shown together, the penalty and NSW interest are together called a "late payment charge". Both are StrataVerze wording, not words of the Act or the SM.",
      "where": "TERMINOLOGY.paymentPlan, TERMINOLOGY.lateChargeGeneral",
    },
    {
      "point": "The Add Property wizard asks for a new building's plan format and saves it with the building. Any listed format can be chosen, as in the building settings, so a standard format plan is accepted and its contributions that include insurance are refused later.",
      "where": "PLAN_FORMAT; src/app/(portal)/adviser/schemes/actions.ts createSchemeAction, src/lib/queries/schemes.ts createScheme",
    },
  ],
